cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GenomeX: unified genome QC — completeness, contamination, and comparative gene content"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it together with the underlying tools."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Hasnat
    alias: Hasnat-GPU
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hasnat-GPU/GenomeX"
abstract: >-
  GenomeX runs Prodigal, HMMER against BUSCO OrthoDB v10 profiles, MMseqs2 and
  fastANI in a single pass over bacterial assemblies, and joins their outputs
  into one report. It scores assembly completeness, detects cross-contamination
  from tetranucleotide composition, GC and displaced single-copy markers,
  distinguishes plasmids and secondary chromosomes from contaminants, and
  partitions strain-unique genes between contamination artefact, genomic-island
  acquisition and divergence. Every judgement is stated against a null:
  composition is scored against windows of the contig's own length drawn from
  the assembly itself, island clustering against a permutation null, and
  marker-duplication thresholds as a rate over the marker set rather than a
  count. Recall is measured against constructed mixtures at known ratios, and
  the limits that measurement exposes are documented rather than smoothed.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - genome-assembly
  - quality-control
  - contamination-detection
  - comparative-genomics
  - pangenome
  - average-nucleotide-identity
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-08-20"
